-- title:
--   Kernel degrees of 𝒪_D-endomorphisms of the base formal module
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r\neq r$, $N$ is a non-zero natural number that is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   The local base consists of a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, together with a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. The unramified cover consists of a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ of it, and the hypotheses that $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that this ideal is maximal, that every element of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, that every monic polynomial over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and that $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$. Finally $v_{\det}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism characterised by `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   The indefinite side consists of rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ has $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is a division algebra at exactly those finite places whose prime contains $r$ or $\bar r$, and of a maximal order $\Lambda$. The moduli data comprise: a scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point-assignment `pt` for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$, and the hypothesis `h𝒳` that this is a coarse moduli datum (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on algebraically closed fields, and the universal property); an auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ coprime to $N$ and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$, a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point-assignment `ptF` for curves with full level-$n$ structure and the fine moduli hypothesis `hM`; a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ and the hypothesis `hρ` that this is a level-twist action (compatibility over the base, the twisting formula, and the label axioms modulo $n$); a forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the point-assignments (`hp_pt`); for each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`) with two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) computing on points the forgetting of the level-$\ell$ subgroup (`hd₀`) and the quotient by it (`hd₁`); and two endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   The definite side consists of rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ has $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and is a division algebra at exactly the places whose prime contains $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, a finite-adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and the height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. Further, $\Gamma^{t}$ is a subgroup of units characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all primes other than $v$; for each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ there are a unit $s_\ell$ and a finite-adelic unit $sf_\ell$ subject to `hs` (four clauses: $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every prime not containing $r$, component $1$ at primes containing $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of that intersection otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), together with $\Gamma^{t}_\ell=\Gamma^{t}\cap s_\ell\Gamma^{t}s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w)=\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   The reduction data comprise: `hΛℤ`, that every rational integer lies in $\Lambda$; a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ with `hcoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the twisted multiplication rule involving $r$ and the Witt-vector Frobenius, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace condition); a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of dimension $2$ over the same ring with `hX₀`: $X_0$ has height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ for $A_0$, and `hA₀`: these identify the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$; families $e,e'\colon\Gamma^{t}\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) with exponents $\mathrm{deg}$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) state respectively: each $e_\gamma$ with $e'_\gamma$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; that scalar $\gamma$ act as the corresponding scalar up to powers of $r$, and conversely that any $\gamma$ acting as an integer up to powers of $r$ is scalar; that for every injective embedding of the centraliser subring of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{X_0.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ has a centraliser element inducing $e_\gamma$ on formal coordinates and mapping to $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; a labelling of the action on the level-$n$ point $P_0$ by elements of $\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; and that every $r$-power isogeny of a geometric fibre preserving level agrees, up to powers of $r$, with some $e_\gamma$. The hypotheses `hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`, `hê`, `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e` (summarised here) provide an order $R_2\le R_1$ whose $r$-power multiples capture $R_1$, an action $\hat e$ of $R_2$ on $A_0$ by endomorphisms over the base which is additive on points, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving, unital and multiplicative, agrees with the $\Lambda$-action on integers, satisfies $\hat e_{\bar x}\circ\hat e_x=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, is compatible with the $e_\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$, and admits a joint embedding statement for $\Gamma^{t}$ and $R_2$ with a single $g$.
--
--   The Drinfeld side comprises: a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special relative to $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`) together with a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects for $\Phi$ to $MD$ and `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is locally surjective); an injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser subring of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ after scaling by a fixed power $r^{m}$ (`hE₀`). The uniformisation datum $eD$, with `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` (summarised here), is a natural bijection, on noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, between the points of $MD$ and pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ and a Deligne datum for $(K_0,\pi)$, matching the structure map, carrying the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action to the twisted action on Deligne data determined by $\mathrm{Fr}$ and $v_{\det}$, carrying $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist, and admitting $\pi$-translates.
--
--   Further: a ring homomorphism $\kappa\colon\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), a natural number $n_0$ and a power-series datum $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`); a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; an Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ for the base point, consisting of $A_{0w}$, morphisms $aw,aw',bw,bw'$ over the base with `hALw` (the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient), `hBSw` (an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` and `hJOINTw` (a joint embedding statement producing, for one $g$, centraliser elements for all $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ and one element matching $aw$ followed by $bw$ and mapping to $r^{k_w'}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$). The datum $\Xi$ attaches to each rigidified curve over a noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent a point of the $MD$-functor, subject to `hΞleg` (its structure map is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ when $B$ is connected), `hΞnat` (naturality under base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves equipped with comparison data) and `hΞdef` (its value is computed by transporting the rigidification along $\theta_0$, $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$, producing an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $j\le 1$ and $\Xi$ equal to the triple given by the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist and $\eta(t)$).
--
--   Finally, $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and the hypotheses `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `hK1`, `hK2`, `hK3`, `hK4`, `hC0e`, `hC0u`, `hnat`, `hG`, `hC2`, `hC2c` (summarised here) state: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds, under $\Xi$, to acting by $r^{c}\,(g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1})$ for some integer $c$; the analogous statement for an $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner pair and $\bar w$ when $\bar r$ is invertible; that $\Xi$ followed by $eD$ and the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action is surjective onto Deligne data over connected bases, injective up to isomorphism of rigidified curves, compatible with base change, and liftable along surjections with multiplicatively annihilated kernel; existence and uniqueness of the normalised transport of $P_0$ to a level-$n$ structure; and a natural transformation $\Theta_f$ from the product of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, the Drinfeld functor $\Omega$ and the constant functor $G$ to the nilpotent points of $f_M$, which is natural, equivariant for $\rho$, and computes $\mathrm{ptF}$ and, after composition with $p$, $\mathrm{pt}$.
--
--   The last group of hypotheses is the transport of endomorphisms from $X_0$ to $\Phi$: $E_X$ is an injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser subring of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{X_0.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$, $N_\beta$ is a natural number and $\beta_0'$ is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ to $\Phi$ (`hβ₀'`) with $\beta_0'\circ\beta_0=\Phi.\mathrm{act}(r^{N_\beta})$ and $\beta_0\circ\beta_0'=(X_0\otimes\kappa).\mathrm{act}(r^{N_\beta})$; and `hEXE₀` states that for every $\varepsilon_X$ in the centraliser subring of $X_0$ there is an element $e_\Phi$ of the centraliser subring of $\Phi$ whose power series equals $\beta_0'\circ(\kappa_*\varepsilon_X)\circ\beta_0$ and with $E_0(e_\Phi)=r^{N_\beta}\,E_X(\varepsilon_X)$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts: for every $\varepsilon$ in the centraliser subring of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{X_0.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$, every $M\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $k\in\mathbb Z$ with $E_X(\varepsilon)=r^{k}\,M$ in $M_2(K_0)$, there exists a natural number $h$ such that, first, the pair of power series underlying $\varepsilon$ has kernel of degree $r^{h}$, meaning that the quotient of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the two components of $\varepsilon$ is a finite and projective $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$-module and that for every field $\kappa'$ and every ring homomorphism $f$ from $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ to $\kappa'$ the corresponding quotient of $\kappa'[[x_1,x_2]]$ has $\kappa'$-dimension $r^{h}$; and, second, the identity of integers $h=4k+2\,v_{\det}(M)$.
--
--   This pins the kernel degree, hence the height, of an $\mathcal O_D$-linear endomorphism of the formal module $X_0$ of the base point in characteristic $r$ in terms of the matrix it produces under the embedding $E_X$: the height is $4k+2\,v_{\det}(M)$ when $E_X(\varepsilon)=r^kM$. It is the $X_0$-side counterpart of the corresponding statement for Drinfeld's special formal module $\Phi$, obtained by conjugating endomorphisms through the isogeny $\beta_0$ and its quasi-inverse $\beta_0'$, and it is used in the comparison of rigidification exponents for transported rigidifications in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve.
